# Commercially-licensed font faces.
#
# Joe Hand IS committed, as of 2026-09-09. It is licensed for web embedding (JOEBOB graphics
# Webfont EULA 1.0, licence owner Southern Destinations, LightSpeed acting as its agent) and
# the §1.3 pageview cap is accepted by the client. It was previously ignored on a
# redistribution reading of §1.5/§1.6 — but nothing placed it, so it 404'd on dev and would
# have 404'd on production at launch. Committing it is the decision that makes the face
# actually work; this repository is private and access is agency + client only.
#
# ⚠️ That decision depends on the repo staying private. If it is ever made public, this face
# must come out and history must be rewritten first. See CHANGELOG.md → Security.
#
# Optima IS committed, as of 2026-09-10, on exactly the reasoning above. SD's web licence
# covers *Optima DemiBold* alone (annually renewable) and the kit arrived that day; the
# single face it licenses ships as assets/fonts/optima-600-normal.woff2. The Monotype
# webfont EULA's transfer restrictions read like JOEBOB's, and the same answer applies —
# private repo, agency + client access, the client is the licence owner — with the added
# point that ignoring it is what made Joe Hand 404 on dev. → LS-2641
#
# ⚠️ Same condition as Joe Hand: this depends on the repo staying private. If it is ever made
# public, this face must come out and history must be rewritten first.
#
# ⚠️ The licence is ANNUALLY RENEWABLE. If it lapses the file must be removed, not merely
# left in place — headings then fall back to Belleza. Diarised on SD's side; noted on LS-2033.
#
# The twelve DESKTOP OTFs in docs/ remain unusable here: that EULA forbids server
# installation and defines OTF→WOFF2 conversion as a Derivative Work. Never convert them.
#
# The OFL/Apache faces (Open Sans, Belleza, La Belle Aurore) are committed and safe to ship.

# Test artefacts
tests/**/test-results/
tests/**/playwright-report/
tests/**/node_modules/
